    "done_when": "running scripts/figures_jt60sa_signals.py, whose diff against main touches only its module docstring (now stating that the flux-loop figure draws FL7 and the 26 differential entries FL1-FL7 to FL27-FL7, FL7 absolute and each differential entry the data dictionary psi_L - psi_7 drawn as stored, the negative of the raw measured difference), in place on the fleet allocation, rewrites docs/figures/jt60sa-signals/jt60sa-E101154-flux-loops.svg and jt60sa-E101031-flux-loops.svg from /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/ids/101154_0.nc and 101031_0.nc, each with 27 panels: FL7 first, then FL1-FL7 to FL27-FL7 (FL7 skipped) in index order, every label and unit read from the IDS; both pf-coil-currents SVGs and both pf-probes SVGs are byte-identical to their committed predecessors; a check script kept in the run's own directory under ~/.config/reckon/crew/runs/ intercepts the traces handed to time_trace_figure_mpl and asserts, for E101154, that the FL7, FL1-FL7 and FL27-FL7 panels equal flux_loop entries 6, 27 and 52 of the run file element for element, its log's first lines naming the expanded command; the evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-signal-figures-from-ids/jtfig-flux-loops-differential.html embeds both new SVGs, each captioned with its run file and the statement that FL7 is absolute and every other panel is the data dictionary's differential flux psi_L - psi_7, stored as minus the raw difference and drawn as stored; ruff check and ruff format --check add no finding on the script",
